            "review_text": "bam n\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam5 contributions\n1\nI had high hopes and really wanted to like this place\nNov 2020 • Family\nHad dinner w the family here last night. Brief rundown. \nStarters: \ncrazy breadsticks: Bread sticks were warm and soft. Marinara sauce that came w it was terrible. There was no thickness to it and was super watery. \nCharlie Hot Buffalo wings. Drowned in some terrible overpowering sauce. \nNuc Mam wings: so bloody dry\n\nMains:\nMeatball sub: not bad. Probably one of the better items on the menu\nSausage pizza thin crust: not bad. Crust was nice, thin, w a bit of a crisp on it that gave it a nice bite. Sausage was ok. Again the tomato/marinara sauce is terrible. \nSaus-eroni deep dish: most disappointing item. Was so look forward to this. Sausage and pepperoni toppings were tasty. Crust and sauce not so good. Not sure if there was supposed to be cheese on this but did not see any on top. \n\nI suppose the biggest issue with this place is everything needs seasoning. Most of the food that came out was so bland. Felt like no love put into the food preparation. Like I said I was so looking forward to this place. Price is pretty affordable. Spend little over 2 million for 7 people. Location is great. Next to river and in some new food alley that will be super hip soon once construction is sorted. Pizza is the biggest disappointment which is sad for a Pizza place.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 20, 2020",
